✅ CSS/SASS/SCSS Topics to Cover
🔹 1. Core CSS Knowledge
Box model (content, padding, border, margin)
Positioning (static, relative, absolute, fixed, sticky)
Flexbox (all properties for containers and items)
CSS Grid layout (tracks, areas, line-based placement)
Display types (block, inline, inline-block, none)
Z-index and stacking context
Media queries and responsive design
Transitions and animations
Pseudo-classes (:hover, :nth-child, etc.)
Pseudo-elements (::before, ::after)
Specificity, inheritance, and the cascade

🔹 2. CSS Architecture & Methodologies
BEM (Block Element Modifier) naming convention
SMACSS, OOCSS (optional but good to know)
Organizing large-scale CSS projects
Avoiding global style pollution
Modular CSS in React apps (e.g., CSS Modules)

🔹 3. SASS / SCSS Features
Nesting (and when not to overuse it)
Variables and color palettes
Mixins (reusable style patterns)
Functions and operators
Partials and imports (\_filename.scss)
Extends and placeholders (%placeholder)
Conditionals and loops (@if, @each, @for)
Maps and lists
Managing themes with SASS

🔹 4. CSS in JS vs Preprocessors
Pros and cons of using SASS/SCSS vs Styled-components, Emotion, or Tailwind
Interoperability with CSS Modules and React
Using SASS with build tools (Webpack/Vite config)

🔹 5. Responsive Design & Layouts
Mobile-first vs desktop-first
Fluid typography and containers
Breakpoint strategies
Utility classes vs component-scoped styles
CSS clamp, min(), max()

🔹 6. CSS Performance & Optimization
Reducing repaint and reflow
Efficient selectors
Minimizing CSS bundle size
Critical CSS and lazy-loaded styles
Avoiding !important

🔹 7. Accessibility in Styling (a11y)
Focus indicators
Reduced motion support
Contrast ratios and accessible color palettes
Hidden content techniques (e.g., visually-hidden)

🔹 8. Styling in React Ecosystem
Using SCSS with Create React App or Vite
Scoped styling with:
CSS Modules
Styled-components / Emotion
Tailwind CSS (utility-first)
Theming with CSS variables or SCSS maps
Dynamic theming (light/dark mode)

🎯 Interview Readiness Tips
Be ready to debug layout issues live (e.g., why flex isn't working, overflow issues).
Understand how to structure styles for large React apps.
Be able to compare SASS/SCSS with CSS-in-JS approaches and explain tradeoffs.
Know how to use media queries, mixins, and variables effectively in a design system.
